My apologies if discussed before: Why can't a char with infravision see
any invisible warmblooded creature? I've found a comment in display.h:

 see_with_infrared()
 
 This function is true if the player can see a monster using infravision.
 The caller must check for invisibility (invisible monsters are also
 invisible to infravision), because this is usually called from within
 canseemon() or canspotmon() which already check that.

This explains how and that it's coded, but not why! Sounds somehow wrong
to me since the invisible monster is still warmblooded and should be seen
with infravision, regardless of his current visibility, in my opinion...

